With the continuous advancement of global economic integration, the changing pattern of international division of labor and the increasingly fierce technological competition, export technological sophistication, as an important indicator to measure the technological content of export products and the upgrading level of a country's export structure, not only reflects the quality of the country's participation in the international division of labor, but also affects the division of labor status and international competitiveness of enterprises in the global value chain to a large extent. As an important part of international trade, the innovation and development of service trade has become an important force to drive the upgrading of export technological sophistication.

In February 2015, the State Council released its Several Opinions on Speeding up the Development of Service Trade and for the very first time, it made systematic plans on how to develop service trade and the priority tasks on its development at the national level. After the introduction of the pilot policy of service trade innovation and development in 2016, the pilot area has been expanding, and the policy has become increasingly influential in the process of service trade development and industrial transformation and upgrading. Under these circumstances, the current paper considers in detail the influence of the pilot policy of service trade innovation and development on the export sophistication of enterprises and develops a theoretical framework of the analysis along three aspects of factor allocation, digital empowerment and technological progress, and investigates the mechanism of policy actions. It is helpful to further explore the policy dividend, and provide empirical basis and practical reference for promoting the upgrading of export technology and improving the service trade policy system.

This study includes China, Shanghai and Shenzhen A-share listed companies over the period of 2012-2023. According to the matching between the location of an enterprise registration and a pilot city of service trade innovation and development, the policy implementation can be considered as a quasi-natural experiment. The multi-period difference-in-differences model is employed to determine the effects of the pilot policy of service trade innovation and development on the export technological sophistication of enterprises, and it is combined with the propensity score matching method. The findings indicate that: (1) The pilot policy of service trade innovation and development has had a positive impact on the export technological sophistication of enterprises and this finding remains true even with several robustness tests; (2) There is a high degree of policy impact regional heterogeneity. Enterprises in western region experience the highest level of promotion under the policy, followed by those in central region and then eastern region; (3) The outcome of the enterprise heterogeneity test confirms that as compared to enterprises not owned by the state and enterprises with poor quality of audits, enterprises owned by the state and enterprises with high-quality external audits are more positively affected by policies; (4) The results of mechanism test show that the pilot policy of service trade innovation and development mainly operates through improving the per capita capital investment level of enterprises, promoting the digital transformation of enterprises and improving total factor productivity, that is, through the factor allocation effect, digital empowerment effect and technological progress effect to promote the export technological complexity of enterprises. 

Based on the research conclusions, this paper believes that the pilot policy system of service trade innovation and development should be further improved, and differentiated policy support should be implemented according to regional differences ; at the same time, we will strengthen targeted support for private enterprises and SMEs with limited capacity to absorb policy benefits, promote the deep integration of digital technology and enterprise production and operation, optimize the efficiency of resource allocation, improve the technological innovation ability and export competitive advantage of enterprises, so as to provide continuous impetus for the high-quality development of China's foreign trade.

Keywords: Service Trade Innovation and Development Pilot Policy; Export Technological Sophistication; Multi-period Difference-in-Differences Model; Total Factor Productivity; Digital Transformation
